  "notes": "Cash-basis county. Governmental funds only (no enterprise funds). Basic statement receipts/disbursements from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements, and Changes in Fund Balances, Total Governmental Funds column (p4). Taxes 3,406,043 split into property/motor vehicle/lodging using the Statement of Activities (p2); Local 933,171 split into charges for services 538,259 + interest 323,376 + miscellaneous 71,536 using the Statement of Activities (they sum exactly). Sale of surplus 49,033 is other_financing. Transfers in/out each 1,356,525 (total column, balanced). Beginning cash is fund balance as originally stated; restated figure (reclassification between funds) is same total 9,485,513. Balance sheet is the Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1); no liabilities. Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p8) used for the General column (more detailed than the combining page, whose General Fund column is not recorded again); budget schedule departments are classified differently from statement functions (it includes capital outlay in functions). Combining General Fund page (p5) used for Inheritance Tax, Emergency Management and Noxious Weed columns. Nonmajor combining (11 funds, p6-7) recorded via Total Non-Major column. Budget schedule for Road/ARP/Highway Buyback recorded; ARP and Road spending split by function from p4 columns. Statement p4 General Fund transfers out (1,225,736) is net of the 40,000 Emergency Mgmt transfer in. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
